Proxmox Backup Server (PBS)

PBS is not a container; it is a dedicated OS. To maximize your R720s, you should deploy PBS as a Virtual Machine on one node, but give it a Physical Disk Passthrough.
Implementation Steps:

    Installation: Download the PBS ISO →→ Create a VM (2 vCPUs, 4GB RAM) →→ Install PBS.
    Storage Passthrough: In the Proxmox Host shell, identify the disk you want for backups (e.g., /dev/sdb). Pass it to the PBS VM:
        qm set <VM_ID> -scsi1 /dev/sdb
    Integration:
        In the PBS Web UI, create a "Datastore" on that disk.
        Go to your Proxmox VE (PVE) →→ Datacenter →→ Storage →→ Add →→ Proxmox Backup Server.
        Enter the PBS IP and the Fingerprint (found in the PBS Dashboard).
    Schedule: Set a "Backup Job" for all critical VMs to run nightly. PBS will now perform incremental, deduplicated backups.
