Layer 2 Stability (STP Configuration)

Since you have a UDM-Pro (UniFi) and TL-SG1024DE (TP-Link), you must manually align the Bridge Priority. The device with the lowest number becomes the "Boss" (Root Bridge).
The Configuration:

    UDM-Pro (Root Bridge):
        Open UniFi Network →→ Switches →→ Select UDM-Pro →→ Settings.
        Set Spanning Tree Priority to 4096.
    TP-Link TL-SG1024DE (Edge Switch):
        Log into Web UI →→ Switching →→ STP.
        Enable STP.
        Set Priority to 32768 (Default).
    The Result: If you accidentally plug a cable from Port 1 to Port 2 on the TP-Link, the switch will see the loop, compare priorities, and instantly shut down the offending port to save your network.

Cable Organization (The Color Code):

    Blue: Trusted LAN (VLAN 10)
    Green: IoT (VLAN 30)
    Yellow: Guest (VLAN 40)
    Red/Black: Management / Switch Uplinks

Labeling:

    Use a label maker to mark both ends of every cable (e.g., JAX-PORT1 $\rightarrow$ UDM-PORT5). This reduces downtime during troubleshooting from hours to seconds.

Power Path:

    Redundancy: If your R720s have dual power supplies, plug PSU1 into the Eaton UPS and PSU2 into the APC UPS. This protects you if a single UPS fails.

